1. Upstream work and dependency
-------------------------------

    MARTINI: Mock Array Radio Telescope Interferometry of the Neutral ISM
    Copyright (C) Kyle A. Oman and contributors
    https://github.com/kyleaoman/martini
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.

astrovodka does not contain a copy of MARTINI. The observation machinery — the
core pipeline (Martini, GlobalProfile), the data cube, beams, noise, spectral
line models, SPH smoothing kernels, angular-momentum coordinates and the
IllustrisTNG data I/O helpers — is imported at runtime from the `astromartini`
distribution, which is a required dependency (see `dependencies` in
pyproject.toml).

astrovodka subclasses MARTINI where its behaviour differs and re-exports the
rest unchanged:

  - astrovodka/datacube.py        DataCube, adding `spectral_unit`
  - astrovodka/martini.py         Martini and GlobalProfile, preserving the
                                  full cube setup across `reset`
  - astrovodka/sources/sph_source.py
                                  SPHSource, adding the redshift distance mode
  - astrovodka/spectral_models.py GaussianSpectrum and DiracDeltaSpectrum,
                                  applying the D_L rather than D_A flux scale
  - astrovodka/beams.py, noise.py, sph_kernels.py, L_coords.py,
    sources/_illustris_tools.py   re-exports of MARTINI's implementations

Because astrovodka is built on MARTINI, it remains a derivative work of MARTINI
and is distributed under the same licence. In accordance with section 5(a) of
the GNU GPL v3, notice is given that the astrovodka-specific layer differs from
MARTINI as follows: cosmological (Planck15) distances replace the linear Hubble
law; the systemic velocity uses the radio convention c*z/(1+z); SPHSource gains
the redshift mode; DataCube gains an explicit spectral-axis unit; and the
spectral models apply the luminosity-distance flux scale. See CHANGELOG.md for
the full history.


